        "creators": [
          {
            "affiliation": "Agile Defense Systems LLC",
            "name": "Davis, Devin Phillip"
          }
        ],
        "description": "<p>Unified synthesis of 7 preregistered hardware campaigns (42 IBM Quantum jobs, 1,062 PUBs, 2,174,976 physical circuit shots, 673 s QPU) across all three 156-qubit IBM Heron r2 processors (<code>ibm_marrakesh</code>, <code>ibm_fez</code>, and <code>ibm_kingston</code>).</p><ul><li>In 40-qubit compilation benchmarks at fixed 39-CZ depth 66 (<code>TMAP-02</code>&ndash;<code>TMAP-05</code>), calibration-ranked vs median path fidelity reversed from +10.54 pp to &minus;4.29 pp four days later due to an unflagged q46 readout excursion (35.0% actual vs 1.1% published), and repeating a pre-job readout-probe selector 82&ndash;85 minutes apart flipped the probe-vs-calibration sign on all three processors while tensored readout mitigation restored calibration-path superiority on all three.</li><li>Longitudinal monitoring and isolation experiments (<code>RO-06</code> and <code>RO-07</code>, 27 jobs, 516,096 shots) show hidden faults (&gt;15% actual vs &lt;3% listed) are transient (6 of 6 recovered below 5%), persist across 15-minute rounds at 87.4% (Fisher OR 1,095), and exhibit &le;1.16 pp multiplexing shift (&le;1.61 pp neighbor state-flip shift), tracing reversals to calibration snapshots static up to 16.0 h rather than readout crosstalk.</li><li>Multiplexed DD spectroscopy across 10 couplers &ge;5 hops apart (<code>CN-01</code>, 499,712 shots) gave null mechanistic contrasts (C_DFS = +0.43 pp, p_Holm = 0.47) while white-noise-only GLS falsely favored a non-local OU bath by Delta-BIC = 10,263 before failing its preregistered 6-coupler held-out gate (p = 0.82); a 550-replicate synthetic audit proves white-noise nulls misclassify 100% of local 1/f dephasing whereas local colored-noise nulls cut false non-local selection to 0%.</li></ul>",
        "keywords": [
          "quantum benchmarking",
          "calibration staleness",
          "readout error",
          "telegraph noise",
          "colored dephasing",
          "dynamical decoupling",
          "IBM Heron r2",
          "ibm_marrakesh",
          "ibm_fez",
          "ibm_kingston",
          "preregistration"
        ],
