        "description": "<p>Algebraic proofs and reproducible SIMULATED benchmarks (<code>provider_job_id: null</code>) calibrated to the 98-qubit Quantinuum <code>Helios-1</code> all-to-all QCCD architecture across non-abelian quantum LDPC coding and pre-submission peaked-circuit classical-hardness gating.</p><ul><li>Proves via group-inversion anti-automorphism and Frobenius / Wedderburn&ndash;Artin duality that unquotiented regular two-block group-algebra (2BGA) CSS codes over F_2[G] satisfy rank(H_X) = rank(H_Z) identically for every finite group G, forcing even logical dimension k (0 violations across 6,480 subset pairs over 11 non-abelian groups).</li><li>Breaking left-right regularity via subgroup-quotient cosets (including D_9/Z_2 with n = 21, k = 3) or symplectic minimum-weight gauge pinning yields 16 odd-k (k in {1, 3, 5}, d &ge; 4) non-abelian CSS codes&mdash;including exact D_9 [[36,3,6]], C_7 x| C_3 [[42,3,6]], and ISD-witnessed C_19 x| C_3 [[114,3,12]] (kd^2/n = 3.7895)&mdash;benchmarked under log-domain Sum-Product BP+OSD-CS decoding.</li><li>Formulates the fail-closed ADV-1 pre-gate requiring candidate peaked circuits to defeat bounded-chi MPS (chi &le; 128), truncated Pauli-path (w_max &le; 4), and causal light-cone (&le; 20 qubits) attacks; appending the 15-CX involution M_6 = J_6 - I_6 (mod 2) eliminates weight-four Pauli leakage and yields 24-qubit and 30-qubit chorded circuits surviving all three classical attacks (predicted Helios-1 peaks 0.3908 and 0.3508).</li></ul>",
        "keywords": [
          "quantum LDPC codes",
          "non-abelian group algebra",
          "two-block group-algebra codes",
          "BP+OSD decoding",
          "peaked circuits",
          "classical hardness pre-gate",
          "Quantinuum Helios",
          "QCCD"
        ],
