        ],
        "description": "<p>Hardware-attested Hayden&ndash;Preskill conditional recovery experiment on a seven-transmon heavy-hex T-junction of the 156-qubit IBM Heron r2 processor <code>ibm_fez</code> (jobs <code>dc1tqaanj2vs73dfrt40</code> and <code>dc23ouqnj2vs73dg3bog</code>; 184,320 total shots, 54 s QPU) measuring the exact 16-operator remnant Kraus trajectory for a continuous non-Clifford three-qubit scrambler <code>U(theta)</code>.</p><ul><li>A universal two-sqrt(X) Euler synthesis locks an identical 28-CZ, 126-SX native gate skeleton with zero routing SWAPs across every angle theta, reducing continuous scrambling sweeps to pure virtual-Z frame updates.</li><li>Six-state conditional recovery rises monotonically from F_6(0 | Phi+) = 0.4964 (P_Phi+ = 0.8913) through peak stabilizer magic theta = pi/4 (F_6 = 0.5998, P_Phi+ = 0.5198) to F_6(pi/2 | Phi+) = 0.8568 +/- 0.0043 raw (0.8771 readout-mitigated, P_Phi+ = 0.2454), exceeding theta = 0 by +0.3602 (t = 62.39, p = 4.54e-6).</li><li>Confirmatory job <code>dc23ouqnj2vs73dg3bog</code> executes all four non-trivial mid-scrambler Pauli-Z twirls inside every randomized block, separating coherent scrambling from dephasing on the identical 28-CZ pulse schedule by +0.1481 +/- 0.0101 (t = 14.61) at 3pi/8 and +0.2283 +/- 0.0149 (t = 15.28, p_Holm = 6.09e-4) at pi/2.</li><li>Includes an offline-compiled [[4,2,2]] codespace companion bundle staged for Quantinuum H2-1 (2,330 HQC).</li></ul>",
        "keywords": [
          "quantum information scrambling",
          "Hayden-Preskill protocol",
          "Yoshida-Kitaev decoding",
          "non-Clifford circuits",
          "Kraus channel",
          "IBM Heron r2",
          "ibm_fez",
          "preregistration",
          "OSIRIS-XTOP-006"
        ],
